  "body": "From #85 (PR #120 review fixes). The per-line cross-hole entry thickens each stock/part facet by a chord-sag allowance computed from its edge neighbours, so a tessellated round is never under-read. A round whose facets do not share vertices (a non-conforming STL, a common export) has no edge neighbours, gets no allowance, and can be read at its chords - the hole mouth up to the chord sag inside real metal and the #84 reach depth short by the same.\n\nDone means: neighbours are found by edge proximity (welded within a tolerance), or facets with no found neighbour fall back to the conservative corner-circle reading; pinned by an unwelded 16-facet round where the entry is at or outside the true surface.",
